cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UCIP or its dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "UCIP: Urban Climate Intelligence Platform"
abstract: >-
  A ward-level heat vulnerability index for Mumbai. UCIP computes a Heat
  Vulnerability Index over a 1 km grid from five indicators built only from free,
  open, global data (Landsat land surface temperature and NDVI, WorldPop
  population density, OpenStreetMap hospital distance and ESA WorldCover
  impervious share), weights them by a PCA on Mumbai's own cells following Reid
  et al. 2009, rolls the result up to the 24 BMC wards with bootstrap rank
  intervals, and suggests nature-based cooling interventions through an
  ecological plantability filter. Datasets, weights, judgement calls and
  limitations are published alongside the output.
